<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32044" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ob-vĭo</span></b> , āvi, 1,
			v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to meet</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 5, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 84, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In a hostile
			sense, <i>to withstand</i>, <i>resist</i>, <i>oppose</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suae confessioni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					39, 5, 30</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To prevent</i>, <i>hinder</i>, <i>obviate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grandini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 35, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vermibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Mart. 10, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
